 # Ftt-Otc-v6 — Agent Log
 
+## 2026-08-12 — PUSH DIAGNOSTICS (auto push still not firing live; v6.11.0)
+
+**Base:** `3df5f1a` (main, v6.10.0). 3 files modified + 2 test suites extended.
+Companion investigation report: `ftt-telegram-bot` PR (arena/019ff4ba…, PUSH_DEBUG_REPORT.md).
+
+### Live evidence chain (2026-08-12 ~06:50 UTC, all verified against the LIVE worker)
+1. `/health` → `version: 6.10.0`, `phase10.pushEnabled: true` → the v6.10.0 scanner-push
+   fix IS deployed and `BOT_TOKEN` **is** set on `fttotcv6` (candidate "secret missing" ruled out).
+2. `phase10.botKvBound: true`, `subscriberCount: 1` → the worker's BOT_KV binding resolves
+   and `auto_users` parses as a 1-element array (namespace/shape mismatch ruled out for the index).
+3. `scanCache` ages ~296s / 14 pairs → the `*/5` scanner is alive and writing `latest:`.
+4. `/api/history` shows FRESH tradeable rows saved today (each = a new non-deduped row, so
+   `saveAndPush` → `pushSignalToSubscribers` RAN for each): XRP/USD SELL 73% B 06:15Z,
+   EUR/USD SELL 85% A+ 02:20Z, BNB BUY 77% 00:25Z, DOGE BUY 77% 01:20Z, AUD/USD BUY 77% 00:40Z.
+5. `phase10.pushesLast24h: 0` → no `pushLog:` key exists → **every push attempt in ≥24h
+   ended with `pushed: 0`** and left NO trace: 'no-token'/'no-match' return silently and send
+   failures only console.warn. The break is inside `pushSignalToSubscribers`, after the token
+   check, before the pushLog write — and it is completely unqueryable.
+6. Deploy pipeline: GitHub Actions deploys have failed since 2026-08-07 06:06Z (wrangler step,
+   npx exit 1) — the leaked Cloudflare token `cfut_pTef5…` was rotated; the repo secret is
+   stale. Live bundles are deployed manually (redeploy.sh / bot_deploy2.sh), which is how the
+   live worker is 6.10.0 and the live bot is v4.5.0.
+
+### Why "200+/day → ~3/day"
+Until bot v4.4.1 the BOT's own autoScan pushed via the BOT token (200+/day). v4.4.2 silenced
+autoScan and v4.5.0 (live) removed it — delivery now depends 100% on worker push, which has
+been failing silently. The ~3/day are the user's own manual bot commands (bot replies work).
+
+### Fix — never silent again
+- `pushSignalToSubscribers` now records EVERY actionable attempt to KV:
+  `pushDiag:last` (overwritten) + `pushDiag:<signalId>` (48h TTL), with the exact outcome:
+  skip reason, per-subscriber gate breakdown (pair/conf/grade/AI), or the Telegram
+  status+body preview on a failed send.
+- `getMatchingSubscribers(signal, env, diagOut)` optionally returns the per-cid gate breakdown.
+- `sendTelegramMessage` errors now carry `.status` and `.body` (200-char preview).
+- `getPushStats` exposes `lastPushDiag` and `pushDisabledReason`; `/health` shows them.
+- The silent `no-token` / `no-match` / send-failure paths now console.warn (rate-limited to
+  once per 15 min per reason).
+- Next fresh tradeable signal on the live worker → `/health` `phase10.lastPushDiag` names the
+  exact gate or HTTP status. If it says `no-token` → set the secret; if a gate → fix settings;
+  if `Telegram 401` → the worker's BOT_TOKEN value is stale.
+
+### Verification
+- `phase10_integration.mjs` 19 → **41/41** (new §"push diagnostics" pins: success writes
+  pushDiag:last + pushDiag:<id>; no-token records the reason + pushDisabledReason; unwatched
+  pair records the gate breakdown; aiOnlyMode + BOTH_UNAVAILABLE records ai:false; Telegram
+  401 records status+body; the REAL handleSignalRaw chain leaves a diag trail end-to-end).
+- `phase10_smoke.mjs` 61 → **64/64** (health block: lastPushDiag + pushDisabledReason).
+- `fix_tests` **281/281** · `r71_tests` **117/117** · `d2_tests` 39 · `probe_tests` 34 ·
+  `fx_mode_tests` 20 · `entry_hit_tests` 7 · `phase7_integration` 36 · `phase7_smoke` 68 · r71 smoke.
+
+---
